# The loop header tests the length of the array, and one iteration stores zero to `length`.
# The store is an operation that declares what it writes, so the loop gets its specialized version, and the length is read in every iteration.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeInvariantArrayStorage: the iterations of a loop are assumed to leave the storage of arrays, and therefore their lengths, unchanged.
# The loop runs as many iterations as the array had elements. No iteration reads an element.
# testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges) and testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) each check the hoisted values against the cell inside the iteration.
